{%- comment -%}
  Organization JSON-LD. Site-wide, in <head>, once.

  Declares MamaJoy as an entity separate from any one page — the raw
  material for a brand SERP feature or a knowledge panel, neither of which
  Google can build from a Product node alone.

  Deliberately narrow: name, url, email and the registered address, because
  those are the only facts that are both true and already public. No logo
  (no confirmed asset URL), no sameAs (no verified social profile URLs), no
  telephone (that number is the store's billing contact, not a public
  support line). Absent is safer than wrong — adding any of the four back in
  is a one-line change once each is confirmed.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign brand = settings.brand_name | default: shop.name -%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Organization",
  "name": {{ brand | json }},
  "url": {{ shop.url | json }},
  "email": "contact@mamajoy.in",
  "address": {
    "@type": "PostalAddress",
    "addressLocality": "Raipur",
    "addressRegion": "Chhattisgarh",
    "addressCountry": "IN"
  }
}
</script>
